 "seesTitle": "What Port de Valldemossa sees",
 "seesHTML": "The cleanest horizon of any rated spot: from the 80 m bluff above the cove, the entire band from azimuth 282\u00b0 to 308\u00b0 is open Mediterranean \u2014 nothing stands above the dipped horizon anywhere the sun will be. Totality rides \u22482.4\u00b0 over the water and the crescent sets cleanly into the sea at \u224820:48. The constraints are on land: one hairpin road down, a handful of parking spots, and cliffs at your back after dark.",
 "capHTML": "Horizon panorama from Port de Valldemossa: terrain silhouettes with projected angular altitudes against the sun's descent. The crescent is last visible at \u224820:48.",
 "recoTitle": "Around Port de Valldemossa",
 "recoHTML": "<li><b>The bluff over the cove</b> \u2014 arrive very early; consider parking high and walking down.</li><li><b>Mirador de sa Foradada / Son Marroig</b> (10 min on the Ma-10) \u2014 same geometry, far more parking (click its row).</li><li><b>Avoid Valldemossa town</b> \u2014 it sits in a valley behind the Teix massif, fully blocked.</li>",
 "verdictText": "Full show \u2014 totality, then the crescent sets into the sea at \u224820:48"
